  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "OpenTelemetry (OTel) is a vendor-neutral framework for collecting traces, metrics, and logs. It provides a single API and SDK for all signals."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "OpenTelemetry",
            "definition": "A vendor-neutral observability framework."
          },
          {
            "term": "OTel SDK",
            "definition": "The software development kit for instrumentation."
          },
          {
            "term": "OTel Collector",
            "definition": "A central agent that receives, processes, and exports telemetry."
          },
          {
            "term": "Exporter",
            "definition": "A component that sends telemetry to a backend."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "OTel Components"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "API: instrumentation interface",
          "SDK: implementation of the API",
          "Collector: receives, processes, exports",
          "Exporters: send to backends (Jaeger, Prometheus)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Benefits"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Vendor-neutral (avoid lock-in)",
          "Single API for traces, metrics, logs",
          "Auto-instrumentation for many frameworks",
          "Large ecosystem"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "OTel Collector"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The OTel Collector receives telemetry from services, processes it (filtering, sampling, enrichment), and exports to backends. It can run as an agent or gateway."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Auto-Instrumentation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "OTel provides auto-instrumentation for popular frameworks (ASP.NET Core, Node.js, etc.). This captures HTTP calls, database calls, and messaging without code changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
      "data": {
        "id": "msa-otel",
        "caption": "OpenTelemetry Architecture",
        "definition": "flowchart TD\n    SvcA[Service A] -->|OTLP| Collector[OTel Collector]\n    SvcB[Service B] -->|OTLP| Collector\n    SvcC[Service C] -->|OTLP| Collector\n    Collector -->|Export| Jaeger[(Jaeger)]\n    Collector -->|Export| Prom[(Prometheus)]\n    Collector -->|Export| Loki[(Loki)]"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Best Practices"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Design for failure",
          "Keep services loosely coupled",
          "Monitor and observe everything",
          "Automate testing and deployment"
        ]
      }
    },
